  "Question": "Which of the following is equal to the product \\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\dfrac{8}{4} \\cdot \\dfrac{12}{8} \\cdot \\dfrac{16}{12} \\\\ &\\quad \\cdots \\dfrac{4n + 4}{4n} \\cdots \\dfrac{2008}{2004}? \\end{aligned} \\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(251\\)",
    "B": "\\(502\\)",
    "C": "\\(1004\\)",
    "D": "\\(2008\\)",
    "E": "\\(4016\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Each numerator except the last is the denominator of the next fraction. Combining the fractions makes these cancellations visible:\n\\[\n\\frac{8\\cdot12\\cdot16\\cdots2004\\cdot2008}\n{4\\cdot8\\cdot12\\cdots2000\\cdot2004}.\n\\]\nEvery multiple of \\(4\\) from \\(8\\) through \\(2004\\) occurs once above and once below. All these factors are positive, so they may be canceled. Only the first denominator and last numerator remain, giving\n\\[\n\\frac{2008}{4}=502.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(502\\), choice B.",
